1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,056
A mushroom on the lawn.

2
00:00:02,056 --> 00:00:04,437
A green speck swimming in pond water.

3
00:00:04,437 --> 00:00:06,526
The bacteria that set your curd.

4
00:00:06,926 --> 00:00:08,133
Plant or animal?

5
00:00:08,133 --> 00:00:09,948
None of them fits cleanly.

6
00:00:10,398 --> 00:00:14,109
Diya found a mushroom in the
college garden after the rain.

7
00:00:14,109 --> 00:00:17,925
It grows from the soil and
never moves, just like a plant.

8
00:00:18,275 --> 00:00:21,573
Yet biologists say a
mushroom is not a plant.

9
00:00:21,573 --> 00:00:22,473
Why?

10
00:00:22,576 --> 00:00:26,716
By the end, you will know the seven
questions scientists ask before they

11
00:00:26,716 --> 00:00:30,574
place a living thing, and why
the old two kingdom system broke.

12
00:00:31,224 --> 00:00:34,466
People have sorted living
things for a very long time.

13
00:00:34,816 --> 00:00:37,538
Aristotle made the first scientific try.

14
00:00:37,538 --> 00:00:42,148
He sorted plants by their simple
form into trees, shrubs and herbs.

15
00:00:42,598 --> 00:00:47,010
He split animals into two groups: those
with red blood, and those without.

16
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:50,389
Much later, Linnaeus
used just two kingdoms.

17
00:00:50,389 --> 00:00:53,367
Plantae for plants, and
Animalia for animals.

18
00:00:54,017 --> 00:00:56,852
Let's run the two kingdom
sort, and watch it break.

19
00:00:57,202 --> 00:00:59,409
A mango tree goes into Plantae.

20
00:00:59,409 --> 00:01:01,249
A cat goes into Animalia.

21
00:01:01,249 --> 00:01:02,149
Easy.

22
00:01:02,271 --> 00:01:05,521
A mushroom does not move,
so it was put in Plantae.

23
00:01:05,521 --> 00:01:08,999
But it has no chlorophyll,
and cannot make its own food.

24
00:01:09,499 --> 00:01:11,704
A bacterium went into Plantae too.

25
00:01:11,704 --> 00:01:14,072
But its cell has no nucleus at all.

26
00:01:14,572 --> 00:01:18,541
And Euglena is green like a
plant, but swims like an animal.

27
00:01:18,541 --> 00:01:19,994
It fits neither box.

28
00:01:20,494 --> 00:01:23,419
So two boxes mixed up
three big differences.

29
00:01:23,769 --> 00:01:27,208
First, cells with a true
nucleus, and cells without one.

30
00:01:27,958 --> 00:01:31,878
Second, living things made of
one cell, and those made of many.

31
00:01:32,628 --> 00:01:36,232
Third, green algae that make
food, and fungi that cannot.

32
00:01:36,232 --> 00:01:37,794
Both were called plants.

33
00:01:38,544 --> 00:01:40,927
Now let's settle the mushroom question.

34
00:01:40,927 --> 00:01:43,036
Zoom in, one level at a time.

35
00:01:43,386 --> 00:01:44,715
Here is the mushroom.

36
00:01:44,715 --> 00:01:47,296
A cap, gills under the cap, and a stalk.

37
00:01:47,796 --> 00:01:48,696
Zoom in.

38
00:01:48,534 --> 00:01:52,820
The whole mushroom is made of thin
threads called hyphae, packed tightly

39
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:53,720
together.

40
00:01:53,549 --> 00:01:55,371
No leaves, no true roots.

41
00:01:55,871 --> 00:01:56,771
Zoom again.

42
00:01:56,761 --> 00:02:00,604
One hypha is a tube of cells,
with nuclei and cross walls.

43
00:02:00,604 --> 00:02:03,033
But look, there are no chloroplasts.

44
00:02:03,033 --> 00:02:05,269
It cannot make food from sunlight.

45
00:02:05,769 --> 00:02:07,202
Zoom into the wall.

46
00:02:07,202 --> 00:02:09,871
A plant cell wall is made of cellulose.

47
00:02:09,871 --> 00:02:14,391
A mushroom's wall is made of chitin,
the same tough material found in an

48
00:02:14,391 --> 00:02:15,964
insect's outer skeleton.

49
00:02:16,614 --> 00:02:18,612
So what do biologists check?

50
00:02:18,612 --> 00:02:19,657
Seven things.

51
00:02:19,657 --> 00:02:21,193
Each one is a test.

52
00:02:21,543 --> 00:02:22,443
One.

53
00:02:22,094 --> 00:02:23,034
Cell type.

54
00:02:23,034 --> 00:02:27,927
Is it a simple prokaryotic cell, or
a eukaryotic cell with parts wrapped

55
00:02:27,927 --> 00:02:29,029
in membranes?

56
00:02:29,779 --> 00:02:30,679
Two.

57
00:02:30,246 --> 00:02:31,146
Cell wall.

58
00:02:31,044 --> 00:02:33,748
Is there a wall, and what is it made of?

59
00:02:34,498 --> 00:02:35,398
Three.

60
00:02:35,138 --> 00:02:36,418
Nuclear membrane.

61
00:02:36,418 --> 00:02:40,854
Is the DNA kept inside a membrane,
or lying loose in the cell?

62
00:02:41,604 --> 00:02:42,504
Four.

63
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:43,484
Body organisation.

64
00:02:43,484 --> 00:02:46,853
One cell, loose threads,
or tissues and organs?

65
00:02:47,603 --> 00:02:48,503
Five.

66
00:02:48,181 --> 00:02:49,552
Mode of nutrition.

67
00:02:49,552 --> 00:02:51,521
Does it make its own food?

68
00:02:51,521 --> 00:02:52,995
That is autotrophic.

69
00:02:52,995 --> 00:02:55,387
Or does it take food from others?

70
00:02:55,387 --> 00:02:56,965
That is heterotrophic.

71
00:02:57,715 --> 00:02:58,615
Six.

72
00:02:58,197 --> 00:02:59,104
Reproduction.

73
00:02:59,104 --> 00:03:01,248
How does it make more of itself?

74
00:03:01,248 --> 00:03:03,611
Spores, seeds, or simple splitting?

75
00:03:04,361 --> 00:03:05,261
Seven.

76
00:03:05,015 --> 00:03:06,861
Phylogenetic relationships.

77
00:03:06,861 --> 00:03:09,500
Which groups share a common ancestor?

78
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:13,073
Phylogeny means the family
history of living things.

79
00:03:13,823 --> 00:03:16,592
The first test splits all of life in two.

80
00:03:16,592 --> 00:03:17,586
Let's compare.

81
00:03:17,936 --> 00:03:22,573
A prokaryotic cell, like the bacterium
in curd, is small and simple.

82
00:03:22,573 --> 00:03:24,035
Its DNA lies loose.

83
00:03:24,035 --> 00:03:26,064
There is no nuclear membrane.

84
00:03:26,514 --> 00:03:31,665
A eukaryotic cell, like a yeast cell,
keeps its DNA inside a nucleus, wrapped

85
00:03:31,665 --> 00:03:36,234
in a nuclear membrane, and has other
parts wrapped in membranes too.

86
00:03:36,834 --> 00:03:37,793
Your turn.

87
00:03:37,793 --> 00:03:41,244
Cyanobacteria are green
and make their own food.

88
00:03:41,244 --> 00:03:44,121
Is their cell prokaryotic or eukaryotic?

89
00:03:44,121 --> 00:03:45,532
Pause and decide.

90
00:03:48,732 --> 00:03:49,749
Prokaryotic!

91
00:03:49,749 --> 00:03:51,737
Cyanobacteria are bacteria.

92
00:03:51,737 --> 00:03:55,021
Being green does not
give a cell a nucleus.

93
00:03:55,671 --> 00:03:56,707
Remember this.

94
00:03:56,707 --> 00:04:00,204
Classify by the cell and
the food, not by the looks.

95
00:04:00,804 --> 00:04:02,457
Now, a worked example.

96
00:04:02,457 --> 00:04:05,870
Let's sort five living things
with just four questions.

97
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:07,245
Question one.

98
00:04:07,245 --> 00:04:09,206
Is there a nuclear membrane?

99
00:04:09,206 --> 00:04:11,116
The curd bacterium says no.

100
00:04:11,116 --> 00:04:13,036
It drops into its own box.

101
00:04:13,486 --> 00:04:14,572
Question two.

102
00:04:14,572 --> 00:04:16,222
Is it a single cell?

103
00:04:16,222 --> 00:04:17,584
Euglena says yes.

104
00:04:17,584 --> 00:04:19,937
A box for one celled eukaryotes.

105
00:04:20,387 --> 00:04:21,517
Question three.

106
00:04:21,517 --> 00:04:23,445
Does it make its own food?

107
00:04:23,445 --> 00:04:25,211
The mango tree says yes.

108
00:04:25,661 --> 00:04:26,715
Question four.

109
00:04:26,715 --> 00:04:28,389
Is there a chitin wall?

110
00:04:28,389 --> 00:04:29,955
The mushroom says yes.

111
00:04:29,955 --> 00:04:32,250
The cat has no cell wall at all.

112
00:04:32,750 --> 00:04:35,528
Five living things, five boxes, not two.

113
00:04:36,178 --> 00:04:37,644
Now, the exam trap.

114
00:04:37,994 --> 00:04:41,781
Many students think, it has a
cell wall, so it must be a plant.

115
00:04:42,181 --> 00:04:44,566
But bacteria and fungi have walls too.

116
00:04:44,566 --> 00:04:48,918
What the wall is made of matters,
and plants also make their own food.

117
00:04:49,568 --> 00:04:51,063
Where is this asked?

118
00:04:51,063 --> 00:04:55,607
As statements on why the two kingdom
system failed, or on which features

119
00:04:55,607 --> 00:04:57,152
are used to classify.

120
00:04:57,752 --> 00:04:58,969
Exam level now.

121
00:04:58,969 --> 00:05:00,764
Read the four statements.

122
00:05:00,764 --> 00:05:02,455
Which ones are correct?

123
00:05:02,455 --> 00:05:03,724
Pause and solve.

124
00:05:09,124 --> 00:05:10,397
The answer is A.

125
00:05:10,397 --> 00:05:12,113
Statements two and three.

126
00:05:12,613 --> 00:05:13,690
One is wrong.

127
00:05:13,690 --> 00:05:17,069
A mushroom's wall is made
of chitin, not cellulose.

128
00:05:17,569 --> 00:05:18,834
Four is wrong.

129
00:05:18,834 --> 00:05:22,327
Phylogeny means shared
ancestry, not body size.

130
00:05:22,927 --> 00:05:24,388
Here is your recap.

131
00:05:24,388 --> 00:05:25,889
Screenshot this card.

132
00:05:29,089 --> 00:05:31,926
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

133
00:05:32,326 --> 00:05:33,226
One.

134
00:05:32,832 --> 00:05:34,985
Why is a mushroom not a plant?

135
00:05:35,885 --> 00:05:36,785
Two.

136
00:05:36,364 --> 00:05:39,734
Which three differences did
the two kingdom system miss?

137
00:05:40,634 --> 00:05:41,534
Three.

138
00:05:41,266 --> 00:05:45,182
What is the difference between
autotrophic and heterotrophic?

139
00:05:46,282 --> 00:05:50,188
Next time: one scientist drew
five boxes instead of two.

140
00:05:50,188 --> 00:05:51,740
What goes into each?

141
00:05:51,740 --> 00:05:54,677
We find out in five
kingdom classification.
